#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Definition]
#title[Type of Cartesian Decompositions]

Let $S$ be a finite set. The type of _cartesian decompositions_ on $S$ is defined as
$
  "cart-dec"(S) :-= sum_(A,B : "FinSet")(A xx_"FinSet" B  ~= S).
$
Where $xx_"FinSet"$ is the #local("00DZ")[cartesian product in FinSet].
In #local("00I2")[agda unimath] this type is called `binary-product-Decomposition`.
